I regularly run programs using 8-10GB of temp file space on
1GB physical memory systems without trouble using normal ext2
FS I/O. I'd suggest you run some tests with standard I/O before
deciding if you need something exotic. Nothing like really running
the code to decide if it needs fixing.

The only real trick is making your I/O as regular as possible so
the system caching works for you, not against you. I do leave a couple
hundred MB of memory for I/O caching. The amount would depend on what
your algorithm does to the file.


Wes




