The last milo I built was close to a year ago(wow time flies). I had no
trouble with FMU. I now have space and a bit of free time to try and
rebuild a new milo.

It would be nice to see MILO expanded a bit and than used as the standard
loader for Alpha's. Either that or there should be Linux support added to
ARC/Alphabios and posibly SRM. Since the choices for OS on Alpha is either
OSF/1->DigitalUnix->True64 or Linux. And with NT being no longer supported
there seems little point in having an NT tailored boot loader.

P.S. I am sure that there ore other OS's that have Alpha support but for
the sake of simplicity I am only concerned with the 2
supported(supposidly) by Compaq.

