In preparation to install Linux on my AlphaStation 200 4/233, I pulled
down
Version 7 of the firmware and attempted to update the firmware.
Everything seemed to go O.K.; SRM and ARC seemed to update correctly (I
did the FULL update, then ARC, then SRM.)

However, after the moment of truth - the machine seems to keep cycling,
and dumping what looks like registers or something onto the screen.  It
does print out the initial checks eb..ea..., etc.  But after that's
done, the box starts dumping out stuff like R29, R23 saved.  Goes by a
little too quickly.  I did try Ctrl-P, but no good.

Am I screwed?  Is there a way to re-flash the firmware?  Or is this
something fairly simple to clean up?

Thanks in advance-
  -Mike White




