> Has anyone EVER got a DS-10 to run its ethernet
> adapter at 100Mbit/s, full duplex?

Yes. Two things:

1) Use de4x5, not tulip.
2) Either wire BOTH SIDES (switch, Linux) to BOTH speed and duplex, or
NEITHER.

Most problems like the ones you describe are due to disagreements about
duplex. If you have partial negotiations, all hell breaks loose.

I believe I have a few hundred of each option of (2), neither and both. But
I think all the XP1000s are both. No doubt it depends on the tulip chip
revision.

-- greg




