Hi Michal --
The build itself (ccc, not gcc) barfed.  Keep in mind that on this
box, xdpyinfo said I was running X11R1!!!  Dunno for sure, but that
sounds like I've got some _really_ old libs out there in X-land.

I'm not so sure that we want a native linux object file.  On the linux
box, flash built cleanly outa-the-box.  NS couldn't find it.  If I can
get it to build on DU, would there not be a better chance that DU
NS would be happier with it?  That's just a guess, as the tools are
at least a bit iffy with with non-native binaries.

Another possibility might be to snag and build jibjpeg & zlib
separately.  How does autoconf do with non-gcc worlds?  I'm guessing
there will be multiple challenges here.
-ls-

