>   The Alpha XL series is a comparatively old and slow Alpha system, and 
>   a system that was expressly targeted and sold for use with the Microsoft 
>   Windows NT operating system.  Not Linux.  Not OpenVMS.  Not Tru64 UNIX.
> 
>   I am not familiar with the Proliant line, nor Linux-related plans for it.
> 
>   I would personally view it as rather unlikely that folks here at Compaq 
>   will (officially) make a particular effort to specifically port Linux to 
>   an (old) box such as the Alpha XL series, but somebody (potentiallu within
>   Compaq or quite possibly external) may well decide to add it as a midnight 
>   project -- I would tend to check on this directly with the folks that are
>   more familiar with Linux on Alpha...
> 
>   The "white-box" Windows NT-only Alpha systems programs were canceled 
>   a while back, and with the cancellation of the Windows NT on Alpha.
>   I unfortunately know of few options for owners of an Alpha XL series.
> 
>   I do not, can not, and have not recommended the XL or any of the other 
>   "white-box" (Windows NT only) Alpha systems for use with OpenVMS.
> 
> :Off, topic, I know, but what the heck are we going to do with no supported
> :O/S of any kind for our Alphas?
> 
>   Port Linux to them?
